Requirements: 26   with obligations: 25   deliberately none: 1

[task-01] The measurement harness scores the ways of failing that a review recorded
    against a human-authored reference set. The figure for what the review failed to
    record and the figure for what it wrongly predicted about tests are never combined
    into a single figure.
    -> scores-failures-against-reference-set  [functional/explicit]
       Score the ways of failing that a review recorded against a human-authored
       reference set.

[constraint-01] A reference set states, for each criterion of a labelled case, the ways
    of failing a competent reviewer should record. Each carries an identifier, a
    classification drawn from the same fixed vocabulary the review uses, a free-text
    description, and the tests that would fail if the delivered code contained it.
    -> reference-set-records-failing-ways  [functional/explicit]
       A reference set states, for each criterion of a labelled case, the ways of
       failing a competent reviewer should record.
    -> recorded-failing-way-entry-fields  [functional/explicit]
       Each recorded way of failing carries an identifier, a classification drawn from
       the same fixed vocabulary the review uses, a free-text description, and the tests
       that would fail if the delivered code contained it.

[constraint-02] A criterion for which no way of failing is plausible carries that fact
    and the reason, and stays distinguishable from a criterion the reference set says
    nothing about.
    -> no-plausible-failure-criterion-distinct-from-silent-criterion  [invariant/explicit]   (also serves completion-03)
       A criterion with no plausible way of failing is recorded with that fact and the
       reason, and remains distinguishable from a criterion the reference set says
       nothing about.

[constraint-03] A reference set naming a criterion its case does not define, or naming a
    test its case does not supply, is rejected rather than loaded.
    -> reject-unmatched-reference-set-entries  [error_handling/explicit]
       A reference set that names a criterion its case does not define, or names a test
       its case does not supply, is rejected rather than loaded.

[constraint-04] A recorded way of failing is matched to a labelled one by what the two
    describe, not by their wording, and each side takes part in at most one match.
    -> recorded-vs-labelled-match-by-described-content  [functional/explicit]
       A recorded way of failing is matched to a labelled one by what the two describe,
       not by their wording.
    -> one-match-per-side  [invariant/explicit]
       Each recorded way of failing and each labelled way of failing takes part in at
       most one match.

[constraint-05] Whether a match was found and whether the two classifications agree are
    reported as separate figures.
    -> separate-match-and-agreement-figures  [functional/explicit]
       Report whether a match was found and whether the two classifications agree as
       separate figures.

[constraint-06] The share of recorded ways of failing carrying the vocabulary's escape
    value is reported as a standing figure.
    -> escape-value-share-standing-figure  [functional/explicit]
       The share of recorded ways of failing carrying the vocabulary's escape value is
       reported as a standing figure.

[constraint-07] The share of labelled ways of failing that the review recorded is
    reported for each classification separately.
    -> labelled-share-by-classification  [functional/explicit]
       Report the share of labelled ways of failing that the review recorded separately
       for each classification.

[constraint-08] How well the predicted catching tests agree with the labelled ones is
    reported as its own figure, computed independently of the share above.
    -> predicted-catching-tests-agreement-figure  [functional/explicit]
       Report how well the predicted catching tests agree with the labelled ones as its
       own figure, computed independently of the share of labelled ways of failing
       recorded.

[constraint-09] A figure with nothing to compute from is reported as absent, and never
    as zero.
    -> absent-not-zero-for-empty-figure  [invariant/explicit]
       A figure with nothing to compute from is reported as absent, and never as zero.

[constraint-10] The existing measure of whether two criteria stating the same demand
    receive the same tests is also computed over the tests reached by way of the
    recorded ways of failing.
    -> same-demand-tests-over-recorded-failures  [functional/explicit]
       The measure of whether two criteria stating the same demand receive the same
       tests is computed over the tests reached by way of the recorded ways of failing.

[constraint-11] Scoring runs from recorded material and issues no live call to a model.
    -> no-live-model-call  [functional/explicit]
       Scoring runs from recorded material and issues no live call to a model.

[constraint-12] Every reference set shipped with the harness loads and validates.
    -> reference-sets-load-and-validate  [functional/explicit]
       Every reference set shipped with the harness loads and validates.

[exclusion-01] Producing the ways of failing that are scored, and predicting which tests
    would catch one.
    -> no-recorded-failures-or-predicted-tests  [functional/explicit]
       The change does not produce the ways of failing that are scored, or predict which
       tests would catch one.

[exclusion-02] Any rating, conclusion, recommendation or report the review itself
    produces.
    -> no-review-reporting  [functional/explicit]
       The change does not produce any rating, conclusion, recommendation, or report
       from the review itself.

[exclusion-03] Which criteria the review derives from a mandate, and how it derives
    them.
    -> no-mandate-derivation  [functional/explicit]
       The change does not alter which criteria the review derives from a mandate or how
       it derives them.

[exclusion-04] Judging whether a labelled way of failing is itself the right one to
    expect.
    -> no-judging-labelled-way-of-failing  [functional/explicit]
       The change does not judge whether a labelled way of failing is itself the right
       one to expect.

[exclusion-05] Running any code under review.
    -> no-runtime-code-under-review  [functional/explicit]
       The change does not run any code under review.

[completion-01] Implementation.
    -- no obligation, deliberately
       The requirement is only the section marker "Implementation." standing alone,
       which imposes no checkable obligation.

[completion-02] A test fails when a reference set naming a criterion its case does not
    define is loaded rather than rejected.
    -> reject-undefined-criterion-reference-set  [error_handling/explicit]
       A reference set that names a criterion its case does not define is rejected
       rather than loaded.

[completion-03] A test fails when a criterion with no plausible way of failing is stored
    so that it cannot be told apart from one the reference set is silent about.
    -> no-plausible-failure-criterion-distinct-from-silent-criterion  [invariant/explicit]   (also serves constraint-02)
       A criterion with no plausible way of failing is recorded with that fact and the
       reason, and remains distinguishable from a criterion the reference set says
       nothing about.

[completion-04] A test asserts that a recorded way of failing worded differently from
    its labelled counterpart still matches it.
    -> recorded-failure-matches-by-description  [test_demand/explicit]
       A test asserts that a recorded way of failing worded differently from its
       labelled counterpart still matches it.

[completion-05] A test fails when a disagreement between two classifications is counted
    as a way of failing the review never recorded.
    -> classification-disagreement-not-counted-as-recorded-failure  [test_demand/explicit]
       A test fails when a disagreement between two classifications is counted as a way
       of failing the review never recorded.

[completion-06] A test asserts that the share of labelled ways of failing recorded, and
    the agreement between predicted and labelled catching tests, are computed
    independently of each other.
    -> independent-computation-of-coverage-and-agreement  [test_demand/explicit]
       A test asserts that the share of labelled ways of failing recorded and the
       agreement between predicted and labelled catching tests are computed
       independently of each other.

[completion-07] On a small set whose figures are known by hand, every computed figure
    equals the hand-computed one.
    -> hand-computed-figures-match  [test_demand/explicit]
       On a small set whose figures are known by hand, every computed figure equals the
       hand-computed one.

[completion-08] A test fails when scoring issues a live call to a model.
    -> no-live-model-call-during-scoring  [test_demand/explicit]
       A test fails when scoring issues a live call to a model.
